  "step_3": "The decision reason is about preferring a more right-skewed lottery — one with a greater probability mass on unfavorable outcomes. However, in this case, Lottery B has only a 1% chance of 0 Euros, which is a small unfavorable outcome, and the majority of the probability is on favorable outcomes (97%). Thus, Lottery B is not right-skewed; it is actually left-skewed. Lottery A has no downside. Therefore, neither lottery is right-skewed, so the reason does not apply. The individual's justification is based on preference for certainty and the perception of a small gain, not on skewness. There is no mention of unfavorable outcomes having a large probability or of evaluating skewness. Hence, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The individual did not consider or apply the skewness criterion to make the choice.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
