  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses on the probability of loss and the magnitude of the loss, not on the proportion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. The decision reason prefers the more right-skewed lottery — i.e., the one with a greater portion of probability on negative outcomes. Lottery B has 90% on a loss, while Lottery A has 45% on a loss of 6000 Euros. Thus, Lottery B is more right-skewed. However, the individual does not mention this skewness or the distributional shape. Instead, the individual justifies the choice by comparing the risk of loss — the high probability of loss in B versus the lower probability in A, even if the loss is larger. This reflects a different decision reason (e.g., risk aversion or expected loss minimization), not skewness-based reasoning. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. The comparison of information shows absence of skewness consideration, and the justification is based on loss magnitude and probability, not distributional skewness. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
